-- title:
--   Vélu quotient by a finite subgroup and its kernel ideal
-- statement:
--   Let $q'$ be a prime and let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $q'$ which is algebraic over $\mathbb{Z}/q'$. Let $X_0$ be a Weierstrass curve over $\kappa$ which is elliptic, and assume that the $q'$-torsion of the group of affine points of $X_0$ is trivial, i.e. $q' \cdot P = 0$ forces $P = 0$. Let $H$ be an additive subgroup of the points of the base change of $X_0$ to $\kappa$ whose underlying set is finite. The assertion is that there exist a Weierstrass curve $W$ over $\kappa$, elliptic, and an additive map $\varphi$ from the points of $X_0$ (base changed to $\kappa$) to those of $W$ lying in [`WeierstrassCurve.rationalHomSet`](def/WeierstrassCurve_RationalEnd.html#L28), that is, either $\varphi = 0$ or $\varphi$ is given on all nonsingular points $(x,y)$ with $x$ outside some finite exceptional set by a fixed quadruple of bivariate polynomials over $\kappa$ as $(n_X/d_X, n_Y/d_Y)$ with nonvanishing denominators, such that three things hold: the kernel of $\varphi$ equals $H$; for every elliptic Weierstrass curve $W_3$ over $\kappa$ and every additive $\alpha$ in [`WeierstrassCurve.rationalHomSet`](def/WeierstrassCurve_RationalEnd.html#L28) from $X_0$ to $W_3$ vanishing on $H$ there is $\beta$ in [`WeierstrassCurve.rationalHomSet`](def/WeierstrassCurve_RationalEnd.html#L28) from $W$ to $W_3$ with $\alpha = \beta \circ \varphi$; and [`WeierstrassCurve.kernelIdealSet`](def/WeierstrassCurve_KernelIdeal.html#L10) of $\varphi$, namely the set of elements $a$ of the subring of $\operatorname{End}$ of the points of $X_0$ generated by the rational homomorphisms $X_0 \to X_0$ that factor as $a = \rho \circ \varphi$ for some rational $\rho \colon W \to X_0$, coincides with the set of elements of that subring annihilating $H$.
--
--   This is the existence of the separable quotient of an elliptic curve by a finite subgroup of points in Vélu's explicit form, together with its universal property and the identification of the associated kernel ideal with the annihilator of $H$ in the ring of rational endomorphisms, in Waterhouse's sense. It is used in the comparison of ideals of Hecke-type rings with subgroups in the Čerednik–Drinfeld part of the development, and in the construction of quotients attached to dual pairs.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_WeierstrassCurve_exists_mem_rationalHomSet_ker_eq_and_forall_comp_and_kernelIdealSet_eq.lean

